+/*
+ * SWEET camera: the Mi 9T's (davinci, SM7150 "sdmmagpie", Titan 175) cameras for iOS.
+ * DRAFT -- not built, not run. Port of HackiOS's bsd/dev/redwood_camera.c (OOSEX GANG, APSL 2.0,
+ * hackios-xnu-kernel/xnu/files/bsd/dev/redwood_camera.c); see davinci-ios/camera/CAMERA-PORT-PLAN.md.
+ *
+ * Same architecture as HackiOS: no Qualcomm CAMSS driver stack, no CCI controller, no ISP. One
+ * kernel thread powers the sensor (bit-banged I2C on the CCI pins), programs CSIPHY -> CSID-lite 0 ->
+ * IFE-lite 0 RDI 0 -> write master 0 to write raw RAW10 frames through an apps-SMMU context of ours
+ * into kernel memory, and /dev/sweet-camera hands the frames to mediaserverd, where a userland
+ * FigCaptureDevice (HackiOS camera_device.c + camera_isp.c, ported) debayers on the CPU.
+ *
+ * Everything below is davinci's, from (a) MIUI's device tree (davinci_0.dts + dtbo overlay: cam-sensor@0..3,
+ * csiphy@ace0000.., csid-lite0@acc8000, vfe-lite0@acc4000, cci@ac4a000/@ac4b000, apps-smmu@15000000,
+ * titan_top_gdsc@ad0c1c4), (b) LineageOS android_kernel_xiaomi_sm6150 (camcc-sdmmagpie.c,
+ * gcc-sdmmagpie.c, pinctrl-sdmmagpie.c, clk-alpha-pll.c Fabia, cam_csiphy_1_2_hwreg.h,
+ * cam_ife_csid_lite17x.h, cam_vfe_lite17x.h, davinci-sdmmagpie-camera-sensor.dtsi), (c) the sensors'
+ * CamX module files from MIUI's /vendor/lib64/camera (com.qti.sensormodule.davinci_*.bin), turned into
+ * RWCTAB02 tables by davinci-ios/camera/tools/davinci_camsensor.py and read at run time from
+ * /usr/local/camera/camera-<sensor>.tab.
+ *
+ *   sensor        Android cell  chip (ID @reg)       CCI bus (SDA/SCL)   reset  MCLK (pin)     CSIPHY  VDIG enable
+ *   wide          cam-sensor@0  IMX586 0x0586 @0x16  CCI0 m0 (17/18)     26     MCLK2 (15)     0, 4L   PM6150L GPIO3
+ *                               (or IMX582 0x0582)
+ *   tele          cam-sensor@1  OV8856 0x885a @300b  CCI0 m1 (19/20)     24     MCLK3 (16)     3, 2L   PM6150L GPIO8
+ *   front (popup) cam-sensor@2  S5K3T2 0x3142 @0     CCI0 m0 (17/18)     23     MCLK0 (13)     1, 4L   TLMM 57
+ *   ultra-wide    cam-sensor@3  S5K3L6 0x30c6 @0     CCI1 m0 (27/28)     25     MCLK1 (14)     2, 4L   TLMM 29
+ *
+ *   7-bit slave addresses: IMX586/582 0x1a, OV8856 0x36, S5K3T2 0x56, S5K3L6 0x10 (tables carry them).
+ *   Supplies (all four, DT): VIO = PM6150 L16 (ldoa16, 1.8 V), VANA = PM6150L BOB (bobc1), VDIG =
+ *   PM6150L S8 (smpc8, 1.352 V) + the VDIG enable above (external LDOs), CUSTOM = PM6150L L9 (ldoc9,
+ *   2.952 V). MCLK 19.2 MHz from the crystal for all. CSIPHY's own supplies (L3C 1.2 V, refgen
+ *   @0xff1000) are the DSI PHY's too and on while the panel is.
+ *
+ * Boot-args (nothing is touched without sweetcam):
+ *   sweetcam=1   look only: clocks, GDSC, pins, PMIC regulator status, SMMU, RPMh (reads; the one write
+ *                is GCC's camera AHB branch, so camcc can be read at all)
+ *   sweetcam=2   + power up the sensor, read its chip ID, power down
+ *   sweetcam=3   CSID-lite's test pattern -> IFE-lite -> SMMU -> memory (no sensor)
+ *   sweetcam=4   the sensor's own frames into memory, N frames, then everything down
+ *   sweetcam=5   /dev/sweet-camera for iOS (sessions on demand)
+ *   sweetcam_sensor=ultra|front|wide|tele (default ultra), sweetcam_mode=N, sweetcam_settle=N,
+ *   sweetcam_pattern=1|2 (sensor / CSID colour bars), sweetcam_frames=N, sweetcam_after=SECS (20),
+ *   sweetcam_rails=0 (do not vote RPMh rails: assume the bootloader left them on),
+ *   sweetcam_fake=1 (with =5: synthetic frames, no hardware touched -- tests the iOS side alone),
+ *   sweetcam_swapi2c=1 (if SDA/SCL turn out the other way round).
+ *
+ * Safety rules kept from HackiOS: only DT voltages; only the registers named here are written; every
+ * write that should read back is read back; any fault -> everything switched off in reverse order and
+ * nothing more for the rest of the boot; whatever was found on is left on. sweet_camera_quiesce() puts
+ * everything down at halt/restart (call it from sweet_halt_restart()).
+ */
